WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:08.040
We learned this morning that an additional
6.6 million people have lost jobs and filed

00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:09.600
for unemployment benefits.

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:14.219
Now the real numbers are actually much worse
than the official numbers.

00:00:14.219 --> 00:00:16.180
And I'll explain why in a moment.

00:00:16.180 --> 00:00:20.820
You might remember that two weeks ago we learned
that in the prior week, 3.3 million people

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:22.630
lost their jobs.

00:00:22.630 --> 00:00:29.070
Last week, we learned that the week before,
six point eight million people filed for unemployment.

00:00:29.070 --> 00:00:36.160
And today we learned that last week, 6.6 million
more people filed for unemployment benefits.

00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:43.600
That now gets us to sixteen point seven million
people losing their jobs and filing for unemployment

00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:45.790
benefits in just three weeks.

00:00:45.790 --> 00:00:51.770
Now, to understand the magnitude of this,
the labor force was right around 158 million

00:00:51.770 --> 00:00:53.760
before this started.

00:00:53.760 --> 00:00:58.900
That means 10 percent of the labor force has
filed for unemployment benefits in the last

00:00:58.900 --> 00:00:59.900
three weeks.

00:00:59.900 --> 00:01:03.030
Now, the question is, can we trust that number?

00:01:03.030 --> 00:01:04.430
Well, we can trust it.

00:01:04.430 --> 00:01:05.860
But the real number is much higher.

00:01:05.860 --> 00:01:06.860
Why?

00:01:06.860 --> 00:01:11.280
Well, number one, there are tons of people
who lost a job but don't qualify for unemployment

00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:12.280
benefits.

00:01:12.280 --> 00:01:15.340
Not every type of job necessarily qualifies
for unemployment benefits.

00:01:15.340 --> 00:01:19.570
There are people who are working under the
table, as the phrase may be.

00:01:19.570 --> 00:01:22.650
There are people in certain jobs where you
don't qualify for unemployment benefits.

00:01:22.650 --> 00:01:24.000
So the real number is higher.

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:29.909
And number two, the systems for filing have
been so overwhelmed that there are tons of

00:01:29.909 --> 00:01:33.210
people who have been trying to file but couldn't.

00:01:33.210 --> 00:01:37.700
Unemployment is administered, managed at the
state level like we have the department in

00:01:37.700 --> 00:01:42.640
Massouda, Massachusetts, Department of Employment
that manages Massachusetts unemployment.

00:01:42.640 --> 00:01:47.360
The Web sites are often not up to the task
of handling the increased traffic.

00:01:47.360 --> 00:01:49.810
The phone systems are often collapsing.

00:01:49.810 --> 00:01:53.450
So there are lots of people who have been
trying to file but haven't been able to.

00:01:53.450 --> 00:01:59.090
So in early May, the April unemployment report
is going to be released and it could conceivably

00:01:59.090 --> 00:02:03.840
hit 15 percent unemployment, which would be
historically high.

00:02:03.840 --> 00:02:09.220
I mean, you have to go back to the Great Depression
era where you had, you know, 25 percent in

00:02:09.220 --> 00:02:11.170
1933.

00:02:11.170 --> 00:02:16.010
We've not seen numbers like that, 15, maybe
even we can get to 20 percent since these

00:02:16.010 --> 00:02:17.280
are tragic numbers.

00:02:17.280 --> 00:02:21.470
It's going to take a long time to recover
regardless of Trump saying it's going to go

00:02:21.470 --> 00:02:25.310
up like a rocket and we're going to be reinstating
everything very quickly.

00:02:25.310 --> 00:02:30.530
A lot of jobs are not going to be reinstated
as the economy starts to open back up.

00:02:30.530 --> 00:02:33.840
Many restaurants and other businesses are
not coming back.

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:35.730
They are closed for good.

00:02:35.730 --> 00:02:37.330
It's going to be a long process.

00:02:37.330 --> 00:02:41.940
Many people will be starting essentially from
scratch, looking for new jobs.

00:02:41.940 --> 00:02:43.820
Now, a few reminders.

00:02:43.820 --> 00:02:45.200
Here is Donald Trump's press.

00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:46.200
I'm sorry.

00:02:46.200 --> 00:02:52.500
Commerce Secretary Wilbur Ross saying just
weeks ago that Corona virus will be good for

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:56.700
the economy while giving us a hacking cough
as he says it.

00:02:56.700 --> 00:02:57.700
Take a look.

00:02:57.700 --> 00:03:03.680
But I want to talk about a victory lap over
a very unfortunate, very malignant disease.

00:03:03.680 --> 00:03:10.709
But the fact is that does give businesses
yet another thing to consider when they go

00:03:10.709 --> 00:03:14.510
through their review of their supply chain.

00:03:14.510 --> 00:03:18.069
And top of all the other things, because you
had czars.

00:03:18.069 --> 00:03:21.360
You have the African swine virus there.

00:03:21.360 --> 00:03:23.230
Now you have this.

00:03:23.230 --> 00:03:27.940
That's another risk factor that people need
to take into account.

00:03:27.940 --> 00:03:34.630
So I think it will help to accelerate the
return of jobs to North America, some to U.S.,

00:03:34.630 --> 00:03:36.370
probably some to Mexico.

00:03:36.370 --> 00:03:42.140
So we can add that to the montage of really
clueless people who have no idea what they're

00:03:42.140 --> 00:03:43.140
talking about.

00:03:43.140 --> 00:03:46.849
Now, in the meantime, and we're going to talk
about this in the interview segment today.

00:03:46.849 --> 00:03:50.870
People still haven't gotten their twelve hundred
dollar stimulus checks from reports.

00:03:50.870 --> 00:03:55.730
I'm seeing the unemployment supplement from
the federal government of up to six hundred

00:03:55.730 --> 00:04:03.269
dollars a week still hasn't started in many,
if not almost all of the states that are through

00:04:03.269 --> 00:04:07.040
which people are receiving unemployment benefits,
not to a significant degree.

00:04:07.040 --> 00:04:12.000
Despite Trump's claims during his press conferences
that billions and billions of dollars in the

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:16.100
paycheck protection plan funds have been doled
out already.

00:04:16.100 --> 00:04:21.239
It seems that very few businesses have actually
received any money so far.

00:04:21.239 --> 00:04:23.430
We're months into this thing now.

00:04:23.430 --> 00:04:25.319
And where are those benefits?

00:04:25.319 --> 00:04:26.610
Where is the money?

00:04:26.610 --> 00:04:27.650
These are very ugly.

00:04:27.650 --> 00:04:31.599
Thursday are made worse by the fact that the
Trump administration has been so brutally

00:04:31.599 --> 00:04:33.419
behind on all of this.

00:04:33.419 --> 00:04:38.229
So we need a government that can actually
behave responsibly and react quickly.

00:04:38.229 --> 00:05:40.830
We don't have it right now.

